Surrogate Measures of Safety
###############################

``tasi.smos`` provides Surrogate Measures of Safety (SMoS) - indicators derived from trajectory data (e.g. time-to-collision
or post-encroachment time) that quantify how close two traffic participants came to a collision, without an actual crash
having to occur. Each example below introduces one metric: what it measures, its formula and literature source, and a
worked example on real ``DLR-UT``/``DLR-HT`` data where the metric's returned value is reproduced by hand from the raw
trajectory data shown.


